# Git commit author

When creating git commits:

- Set the commit **author** (and committer, if you control it) to GitHub user **Philipp0205**, not Cursor.
- Use name `Philipp K.` and email `36603238+Philipp0205@users.noreply.github.com` unless the repo already has a matching `user.name` / `user.email` for Philipp0205.
- If the environment is configured as `Cursor Agent` / `cursoragent@cursor.com`, override it for the commit, for example:

```bash
git -c user.name="Philipp K." -c user.email="36603238+Philipp0205@users.noreply.github.com" commit -m "..."
```

- Do **not** add Cursor as a co-author. Do not include trailers such as:
  - `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>`
  - `Co-authored-by: Cursor Agent`
  - any other Cursor / cursoragent co-author line
- Do not add "Made with Cursor" or similar attribution in the commit message.

```
# BAD
Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>

# GOOD
Author: Philipp K. <36603238+Philipp0205@users.noreply.github.com>
(no Cursor co-author trailer)
```
